595	     *  moves a DRAFT, OPEN or PENDING claim to another person on the sheet. It keeps its date, takes
596	     *  the next number in the sequence it is numbered in (its old one given up for good; a draft has
597	     *  none and gets none), loses any figure a statement bound it to (live again until its new person's
598	     *  next statement), and is listed as its new person's newest claim. Anyone else, a SETTLED or VOID
599	     *  claim, a correction (it names a claim of its own person), a claim dated in a closed period, or
600	     *  a move to the same person or to one retired before the claim's date, is refused. */
601	    @Transactional
